   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Sleeping-beauty pairs — convexity analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Sleeping beauties (dormant, then a late citation burst) should have **convex** cumulative trajectories\n",
    "(low AUC). Using the Ke et al. beauty coefficient `SB_B` from `paper_sb`/`patent_sb`, we (a) show the top\n",
    "sleeping-beauty examples, (b) compare the high-SB average trajectory to the overall, and (c) test whether\n",
    "higher `SB_B` ⇒ lower AUC (more convex). Paper SB → paper (p2p) trajectory (**red**); patent SB →\n",
    "patent (pat2pat) trajectory (**blue**)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "3b8aabdd",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-28T17:34:20.614761Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-28T17:34:20.614761Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-28T17:36:21.415093Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-28T17:36:21.415093Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "<timed exec>:42: DeprecationWarning: `trapz` is deprecated. Use `trapezoid` instead, or one of the numerical integration functions in `scipy.integrate`.\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "high paper-SB: 3,000 paper-traj, AUC 0.431  (overall paper AUC 0.622)\n",
      "high patent-SB: 3,000 patent-traj, AUC 0.307  (overall patent AUC 0.471)\n",
      "CPU times: total: 1min 59s\n",
      "Wall time: 2min\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "<timed exec>:42: DeprecationWarning: `trapz` is deprecated. Use `trapezoid` instead, or one of the numerical integration functions in `scipy.integrate`.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "%%time\n",
    "psb = pd.read_parquet(V.paper('paper_sb.parquet'),\n",
    "                      columns=['paper_id', 'SB_B']).rename(columns={'paper_id': 'paperid', 'SB_B': 'paper_SB_B'})\n",
    "tsb = pd.read_parquet(V.patent('patent_sb.parquet'),\n",
    "                      columns=['patent_id', 'SB_B']).rename(columns={'SB_B': 'patent_SB_B'})\n",
    "\n",
    "# (c) SB for the 20k sample -> per-pair convexity index vs SB\n",
    "selk = sel.merge(psb, on='paperid', how='left').merge(tsb, on='patent_id', how='left')\n",
    "mp_ = selk.set_index(['paperid', 'patent'])['paper_SB_B']; mt_ = selk.set_index(['paperid', 'patent'])['patent_SB_B']\n",
    "paper_cvx = cvx(PM); patent_cvx = cvx(QM)\n",
    "paper_SB = np.array([mp_.get(k, np.nan) for k in common]); patent_SB = np.array([mt_.get(k, np.nan) for k in common])\n",
    "\n",
    "# (a,b) high-SB subsets from the full sufficient-signal population\n",
    "sig = both[(both.p2p_tot >= MIN_TOTAL) & (both.p2p_span >= MIN_SPAN) &\n",
    "           (both.pat_tot >= MIN_TOTAL) & (both.pat_span >= MIN_SPAN)].copy()\n",
    "sig['patent_id'] = sig['patent'].str.extract(r'[Uu][Ss]-0*([0-9]+)', expand=False)\n",
    "sig = sig.merge(psb, on='paperid', how='left').merge(tsb, on='patent_id', how='left')\n",
    "NTOP = 3000\n",
    "hi_p = sig.dropna(subset=['paper_SB_B']).nlargest(NTOP, 'paper_SB_B').reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "hi_t = sig.dropna(subset=['patent_SB_B']).nlargest(NTOP, 'patent_SB_B').reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "hp_mats = traj_matrix(pt, hi_p, 'yrs_since_pub', 'p2p')\n",
    "ht_mats = traj_matrix(qt, hi_t, 'yrs_since_grant', 'pat2pat')\n",
    "HP = np.array(list(hp_mats.values())); HT = np.array(list(ht_mats.values()))\n",
    "print(f'high paper-SB: {len(HP):,} paper-traj, convexity index {cvx(HP.mean(0)):.3f}  (overall paper convexity index {cvx(PM.mean(0)):.3f})')\n",
    "print(f'high patent-SB: {len(HT):,} patent-traj, convexity index {cvx(HT.mean(0)):.3f}  (overall patent convexity index {cvx(QM.mean(0)):.3f})')"
   ]
  },
